ASSISTANT ## Updated assessment (now grounded in the code)
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT The proposal slots into the existing architecture more cleanly than I'd guessed, because the hard plumbing already exists:
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT 1. **The 9p precedent.** `setup.nix` already shares `$DEVTOOLS_CONFIG` read-only via `-virtfs ... readonly=on` and an explicit `systemd.mounts` unit. A repo share is the same pattern with a second `mount_tag`.
ASSISTANT 2. **The env-var-through-the-launcher trick.** `run-nixos-vm` is a bash script, so `$DEVTOOLS_CONFIG` inside `virtualisation.qemu.options` expands at launch time, after the launcher exports it. `$DEVTOOLS_REPO` (or `$PWD`) works identically — and since `nix run` preserves the working directory, the launcher can capture the *live* working tree, which resolves the uncommitted-changes problem I flagged earlier.
ASSISTANT 3. **Overlay in the guest.** Mount the repo share ro at e.g. `/mnt/repo`, then an overlay with upper/work on tmpfs at `/workspace`. Writes copy up locally; git operations work via copy-up; the lower layer stays pristine; diffing upper vs lower (or `git diff` in the overlay) yields the agent's changes. Because git only *reads* through 9p (writes land in the local upper layer), the classic 9p+git flakiness mostly doesn't apply.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT So: viable, and the recommended shape is now concrete: **read-only 9p share of the live tree + overlayfs upper in the guest**.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ## Things the code surfaces that matter for the proposal
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT - **Mount ordering bug (existing):** the comment on `systemd.services.llm-agent` says the service requires the 9p mount, but the unit only orders after `network-online.target` — there's no `after`/`requires` on `run-agent_keys.mount`. Both are merely `wantedBy = multi-user.target`, so the agent can start before the key dir is mounted. This becomes load-bearing once the repo mount exists (the agent will read the repo immediately). Fix: `after`/`requires` the mount units on the service.
ASSISTANT - **Unit-name escaping:** if the repo mount path contains a dash (e.g. `/mnt/repo-source`), the systemd unit name is `mnt-repo\x2dsource.mount` — pick a dash-free path (e.g. `/mnt/repo`) to keep dependencies readable.
ASSISTANT - **Egress is still undefined:** the overlay upper lives in the ephemeral VM, so the agent's changes vanish at shutdown. Cheapest options: a second, writable virtfs share (e.g. under `$DEVTOOLS_CONFIG` or a repo-local gitignored dir) where the agent writes `git diff` output; or have the service print the diff to the serial console (journald already forwards there).
ASSISTANT - **Repo path resolution:** `$PWD` at launch time is the invocation dir, which may be a subdir. `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` in the launcher is more robust — this is why I'd like to see `prelude/config.nix` (maybe the prelude already has a repo-root notion).
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ## Brief sketch of the changes
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT - Launcher: resolve repo root, `export DEVTOOLS_REPO=...` before `exec run-nixos-vm`.
ASSISTANT - `virtualisation.qemu.options`: add `-virtfs local,path="$DEVTOOLS_REPO",mount_tag=devtools-repo,security_model=none,readonly=on`.
ASSISTANT - Guest: `systemd.mounts` entry for `/mnt/repo` (9p, ro) + an overlay mount (or small oneshot) at `/workspace` with upper/work under `/run`; `requires`/`after` chained from the 9p mounts to the agent service.
ASSISTANT - Agent service: point the tools at `/workspace` (e.g. `WorkingDirectory` or an env var).
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ## Files worth adding
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT - `prelude/config.nix` — `devtools-prelude.get-config`, to see what `DEVTOOLS_CONFIG` is and whether a repo-root variable belongs there.
ASSISTANT - `flakeModule.nix` (and/or `flake.nix`) — module wiring; also tells me whether `self` is available, in case you'd ever want the store-path snapshot alternative.
ASSISTANT - `journal/feature/agentic-dev/session-contexts/langchain sandbox/session.md` — the sandbox design intent, likely relevant to how the repo exposure is meant to behave.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT (`lite-llm/setup.nix` etc. aren't needed for this question.)
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT Verdict line: viable, low-risk, incremental; main open design decision is egress.
