ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT # Updated Analysis (now grounded in the code)
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT Good news: the proposal slots into the existing architecture more cleanly than my earlier generic assessment assumed, because the hard plumbing already exists in `setup.nix`.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ## Why it fits
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT 1. **The 9p precedent is already there.** The key directory is shared via `-virtfs ... readonly=on` and an explicit `systemd.mounts` unit. A repo share is the same pattern with a second `mount_tag` — incremental, not new machinery.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT 2. **The env-var-through-the-launcher trick generalizes.** `run-nixos-vm` is a bash script, so `"$DEVTOOLS_CONFIG"` inside `virtualisation.qemu.options` expands at launch time, after the launcher exports it. A `"$DEVTOOLS_REPO"` works identically — and since `nix run` preserves the working directory, the launcher can share the **live working tree**, which resolves the uncommitted-changes problem I flagged earlier (a store-path snapshot would have dropped dirty files and `.git`).
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT 3. **Overlay-in-the-guest is the right COW shape here.** Mount the repo share read-only at e.g. `/mnt/repo`, then an overlay with upper/work dirs on tmpfs at `/workspace`. Writes copy up locally, the lower layer stays pristine, and git operations work via copy-up. Notably, git only *reads* through 9p (writes land in the local upper layer), so the classic 9p+git flakiness mostly doesn't apply.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT **Verdict: viable, low-risk, and the recommended concrete shape is: read-only 9p share of the live tree + overlayfs upper in the guest.**
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ## Things the code surfaces that matter
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT - **Existing ordering bug:** the comment on `systemd.services.llm-agent` claims the service requires the 9p mount, but the unit only orders after `network-online.target` — there's no `after`/`requires` on `run-agent_keys.mount`. Both are just `wantedBy = multi-user.target`, so the agent can start before its key dir is mounted. This becomes load-bearing once the agent reads the repo at startup; fix it as part of this work.
ASSISTANT - **Unit-name escaping:** a mount path containing a dash (e.g. `/mnt/repo-source`) becomes `mnt-repo\x2dsource.mount` in systemd. Pick a dash-free path so the dependency chain stays readable.
ASSISTANT - **Egress is still undefined:** the overlay upper lives in the ephemeral VM, so the agent's changes vanish at shutdown. Cheapest options: a second *writable* virtfs share (under `$DEVTOOLS_CONFIG` or a gitignored repo-local dir) where the agent writes a `git diff` patch; or print the diff to the serial console (journald already forwards there).
ASSISTANT - **Repo path resolution:** `$PWD` at launch time may be a subdirectory. `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` in the launcher is more robust.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ## Brief sketch of the changes
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT - Launcher: resolve repo root, `export DEVTOOLS_REPO=...` before `exec run-nixos-vm`.
ASSISTANT - `virtualisation.qemu.options`: add `-virtfs local,path="$DEVTOOLS_REPO",mount_tag=devtools-repo,security_model=none,readonly=on`.
ASSISTANT - Guest: a `systemd.mounts` entry for `/mnt/repo` (9p, ro) plus an overlay mount at `/workspace` with upper/work under `/run`; chain `requires`/`after` from the mounts to the agent service.
ASSISTANT - Agent service: point the tools at `/workspace` (e.g. `WorkingDirectory` or an env var).
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ## Other files worth adding
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT - **`prelude/config.nix`** — to see what `devtools-prelude.get-config` provides and whether a repo-root variable belongs there rather than in the launcher.
ASSISTANT - **`flakeModule.nix`** (and/or `flake.nix`) — module wiring; also whether `self` is passed, in case you ever want the store-path snapshot alternative.
ASSISTANT - **`journal/feature/agentic-dev/session-contexts/langchain sandbox/session.md`** — the sandbox design intent, likely relevant to how repo exposure should behave.
ASSISTANT 
